  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) RUN HOST MAINTENANCE: From maintenance worklist `command_jobs_wl2`, run the standard disk check ('df -h /') on each host with an ACTIVE maintenance job (skip any job flagged superseded on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists superseded look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then run the command on it. Then, from worklist `set_release_pr_wl1`, record the release pull request on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) ACKNOWLEDGE ISSUES: From ack worklist `ack_jobs_wl2`, post an acknowledgement comment on each OPEN issue awaiting triage (skip closed on its dereferenced record look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then comment on it. Then, from worklist `attach_iam_policy_wl1`, grant the CI deploy user its scoped IAM policy: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) ROTATE SECRETS: From rotation worklist `rotations_wl2`, rotate each CI secret still due for rotation (skip rotated_recently on its dereferenced record look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then set the new value. Then, from worklist `delete_secret_wl1`, remove the decommissioned CI secret: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) RESTART SERVICES: From restart worklist `restart_jobs_wl2`, restart the service on each host with a PENDING restart (skip draining on its dereferenced record hosts). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then restart it. Then, from worklist `close_issue_wl1`, close the resolved tracking issue: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (E) MERGE PULL REQUESTS: From merge worklist `merge_jobs_wl2`, merge each pull request still OPEN (skip already_merged on its dereferenced record look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then squash-merge it into main. Then, from worklist `revoke_security_group_port_wl1`, revoke the stale inbound port rule: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
